sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila takahashii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.362 µm (Pass 1 field render) — MorphoEval overall 77.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Periodic Schnakenberg integration on a 28.344 µm chart (12 × 2.362 µm). Analytic peak λ = 2.3615 µm, σ_max = 0.0743. Numerical dominant wavelength 2.314 µm. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9905, RMSE = 0.0568, KS = 0.0909 on 22 wavenumbers. Equal-diffusion ablation std collapses to ~4e-13 against a patterned std of 0.0475. Dv sweep wavelengths increase from 2.300 to 2.733 µm above onset. Raw Otsu circularity on the gallery plate is 0.0018. GIF is 640×480, 12 frames. CV similarity of the field GIF against the plate is 80.0. Geological age 0 Ma. Overall 77.0/100 (faithfulness 73.7, reproducibility 84.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 948e555fd733650f05998c84112d9f34e837fe61; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-takahashii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 948e555fd733650f05998c84112d9f34e837fe61, image/png, 504856 B, 1512×912 px, artifact_sha256 9a6e864e3a6bbfdfa67faf5c30bb298484d26fa5167529c66e2757e57a85f310 (sha256 9a6e864e3a6bbfdfa67faf5c30bb298484d26fa5167529c66e2757e57a85f310), spec_fingerprint 55cc231a3a77c642a29cd527c03b6d6546b3cf3ea80c82a6ec4a040de441d66a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 55cc231a3a77c642a29cd527c03b6d6546b3cf3ea80c82a6ec4a040de441d66a; artifact_sha256: 9a6e864e3a6bbfdfa67faf5c30bb298484d26fa5167529c66e2757e57a85f310; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_takahashii_specimen.jpg=be067c44d300a455..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c96d7a5d72c78239..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=101832d102fd3942..., datasets/drosophila_takahashii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=9b6681d3a2e6cbf4...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a finite critical wavelength | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics with a cubic autocatalytic term | Murray 1981 wavelength set by the diffusion scale | Tanaka, Barmina and Kopp 2009 and Kopp 2011 on sex-comb diversification | Atallah et al. 2014 on Drosophila suzukii and its close relatives; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters a=0.162, b=1.247, Du=0.042744, Dv=0.971570 placing λ_c at 2.362 µm | Explicit Euler on a periodic 12-wavelength chart and the radial-FFT wavelength | Dispersion Pearson/KS, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation; transfer_boundary: 2.362e-06 m is the campaign detail-scale assignment (log10=-5.627), not a quoted takahashii ocellus measurement | The suzukii → takahashii → teissieri order is chronoseries index 37/41 at 0 Ma, not an anagenetic fossil series; does_not_claim: That a wet-lab paper reports 2.362 µm for a D. takahashii ocellus | That D. takahashii carries the D. suzukii apical wing spot | That the Pass 1 Otsu contour is a usable body outline." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.7]: Field mode stored simulation structure-tensor coherency as 0. Measure it on the composited frame and keep the value distinct from the specimen coherency.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=3.3]: Raw Otsu circularity is 0.0018 because grain fragments the contour. Segment the largest smoothed body component and composite the activator into that mask.",
            "remediation needed: R1. Replace raw Otsu on the grainy plate (circularity 0.0018) with a smoothed largest-component body mask that excludes the caption band.",
            "remediation needed: R2. Composite the lattice inside that mask and record a non-zero simulation coherency distinct from the specimen coherency.",
            "remediation needed: R3. Still one gallery plate and one assessor; do not invent a second specimen or a second scorer." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.77"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

